cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use helios16p in academic work, please cite it as below."
title: "helios16p: the RoboSense Helios 16P LiDAR in pure Python"
version: 0.2.0
date-released: 2026-11-04
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/Sach279/helios16p"
authors:
  - family-names: Sachdeva
    given-names: Akshit
    affiliation: "School of Computing, Engineering and the Built Environment, Edinburgh Napier University"
keywords:
  - lidar
  - robosense
  - helios 16p
  - point cloud
  - ros 2
abstract: >-
  Live UDP decoding, recording, replay, a perception pipeline (ground removal,
  clustering, multi-object tracking) and an interactive 3D viewer for the
  RoboSense Helios 16P, with or without ROS. The decoder applies the sensor's
  own DIFOP calibration and was validated against the vendor driver to a
  fraction of a millimetre. Written during an MRes at Edinburgh Napier
  University, where the sensor provided the metric reference for a thesis on
  non-destructive surveying of traditional Scottish buildings with a nano-UAV.
